  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Radius of nucleus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>Density of nucleus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#961;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Mass</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nucleus</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>volume</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nucleus</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math> &nbsp;Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>: mass of proton or neutron and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>: mass number.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mmultiscripts><mo>&#160;</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p>Hence, density of nucleus is independent of mass number.</p><p>Therefore, the&nbsp;ratio is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
